    {
      "id": "credits",
      "layer": "customer",
      "responsibility": "Credit units, credit grants and holds (G3/G4a). Promotional and paid grants (paid only through an invoice), units with or without a money rate (the second kind keeps a real-time balance row per customer and unit, and pays the usage of a meter that has a credit cost: the credits are taken at ingest and settled against the grants each hour and in the period invoice, with revenue on use), drawdown in a fixed order before and after tax, expiry into breakage, restore on invoice void, credit packs and plan credits on prices, the derived live balance, holds with capture and release (leases: partial capture, extend; in units too), money overage past the balance (a unit or meter price) and an overdraft floor by unit, plan and customer, void after settlement and the full pack refund re-draw, the credit reports (deferred revenue roll-forward, grant activity, runway in units, refused demand), and the access check with the blocking policy ladder. The engine rules are business settings in `credit_config` (policy.ts `resolveCreditEngineRules`; unset keeps the old rule): usage in a trial, customers with no subscription and their overdraft and invoice delay, restored-credit expiry, auto top-up after a hard decline, capture past a hold.",
